{
  "_readme": "Settings for 'Search the Monastery' (دوّر في الدير), the hidden-letters game at the desert monastery. Change numbers here; no code change needed. letterCounts: the levels (how many letters hide). smallScreenWidth: phones (shortest screen side under this) play without the brothers. levelArt: a picture per level tile, by number of letters (tiles without one are drawn in code). heroRunMs: how long the brother takes to reach a found letter. nameBubbleMs: how long the letter's name stays in the bubble. hintGlowMs: how long a hint's glow pulses. tapRadius: how forgiving a tap is (1 = about the letter's size). minSpotGap: two letters never hide closer than this (in scene heights). maxRotation: letters lean up to this many degrees either way. letterColors: muted colours that blend with the scene; each letter gets one at random. letterOpacity: 1 = solid. showSpots: true draws every hiding spot as a circle, to line spots up with new art (keep false for kids). scenes: one room per screen shape; each game uses the one whose shape fills the screen best (wide for tablets and computers, tall for phones), so nothing ever scrolls. The objects' cut-out pictures can be shared by both rooms; only their rect differs. Everything in a scene is in fractions of its picture (x of its width, y of its height, 0 = top left). aspect: the picture's width / height. background: the room picture without the objects (drawn in code when null, in the shape named by id). objects: things standing in front of the letters, each a cut-out picture (image, transparent PNG) placed at rect [x, y, width, height]; without an image the 'shape' is drawn in code. spots: where a letter can hide (its centre x, y and size as a fraction of the scene height). Letters are drawn behind every object, so a spot sits on an object's edge to show only part of the letter. The spots are worked out from the pictures by tools/games/monastery_spots.py: run it again after moving an object or changing a picture. Every game picks random spots and random letters.",
